# Google C++ style (https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html) with the
# project's deviations below.  `make format` rewrites the tracked C++ sources,
# `make format-check` (scripts/format_check.sh, the CI gate) reports drift.
#
# One rule clang-format cannot express is enforced by the same gate
# (scripts/trailing_comments.py): a `//` comment goes on its own line above the code
# it describes, never after it on the same line.  Exceptions: `}  // namespace x` and
# other closing-brace-only lines, `#if/#else/#endif  // …`, `// NOLINT…` and the
# clang-format on/off markers.
BasedOnStyle: Google
Language: Cpp
Standard: c++20

IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 120
TabWidth: 4
UseTab: Never
AccessModifierOffset: -3
ConstructorInitializerIndentWidth: 4
ContinuationIndentWidth: 4

DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
